<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Shrike is distributed directly, without the App Sandbox, so this
        file lists no entitlements. The local install in /Applications is
        signed with the Apple Development certificate; the public DMG is
        ad-hoc signed. Neither is notarized (there is no Developer ID and
        no Mac App Store version). Direct distribution lets users open any
        folder instantly and launch external editors freely.

        Hardened runtime is enabled in build settings, not entitlements.
        Runtime exceptions (JIT, library validation) would be added here
        only if a real feature needs them.

        Do not add `com.apple.security.get-task-allow`: Scripts/lib/common.sh
        rejects it in a signed build.

        The sandbox-only keys that used to be listed here
        (`files.user-selected.read-write`, `files.bookmarks.app-scope`) were
        removed: without `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` they have no
        effect, and the app uses plain (not security-scoped) bookmarks.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
